 "title": "Control Your Mind Through Positive Self-Talk",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator explains that you become what you think about because your brain believes whatever you repeat to it. The main lesson is to stop telling yourself negative things and instead repeat positive affirmations until your brain believes them.",
 "key_points": [
  "You become what you think about.",
  "Your brain does not care if your thoughts are true; it believes exactly what you repeat to it.",
  "Stop telling yourself what you're not (e.g. \"I'm a loser\", \"I can't do this\").",
  "Start telling yourself what you are (e.g. \"I'm the best\", \"I can do anything I put my mind to\").",
  "Say it until your brain believes it, and then watch yourself become it.",
  "If you can control your mind, you control every aspect of your life."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by markos.procopiou. Text / caption: Control your mind. #motivation #mindset. Transcript: and some of the best advice I've heard is that you become what you think about your brain does not care if your thoughts are true it believes exactly what you repeat to it it cannot handle the negative I'm a loser I'm a loser I can't do this stop telling yourself what you're not and start telling yourself what you are I'm the best I'm the best I can do anything I put my mind to say it until your brain believes it and then watch yourself become it because if you can control your mind you control every aspect of your life.",
